AB  - In this study, a machine learning approach was applied to evaluate the impact of operating and design variables on dry powder inhalation efficiency. Emitted dose and fine particle fraction data were extracted from the literature for a variety of drug and carrier combinations. Carrier surface properties are obtained by image analysis of SEM images reported. Models combining artificial neural network and genetic algorithm were developed to determine the emitted dose and fine particle fraction. Design strategies for the carrier surface were also proposed to enhance the fine particle fractions.
