AB  - The concentration of PM2.5 is closely related to air, environmental quality and human health. In this study, an hourly prediction method of PM2.5 concentration in Beijing based on Bi-LSTM neural network was proposed. Firstly, Python crawlers were used to crawl hourly PM2.5 concentration and meteorological information for data fusion, and then Bi-LSTM prediction model was constructed to realize the prediction of PM2.5 concentration. To verify the validity of the proposed method, 2628 h of test data from the test set were used for testing and compared with two different cyclic neural network prediction models based on GRU and Bi-LSTM. At the same time, the validity of introducing meteorological features into the method was discussed. The test results show that the MAE of this research method for PM2.5 concentration prediction was 14.15, which was lower than the other two methods 49.91 and 31.51; the RMSE was 17.20, which was lower than the two methods 60.03 and 36.70; The R-2 was 0.95, which was 0.10 and 0.03 higher than the two comparison methods respectively. Moreover, the method introduced meteorological features, which effectively reduced the prediction error of PM2.5 concentration. The results showed that it was feasible to use this method to predict hourly PM2.5 concentration, and it could provide some reference for air quality assessment and environmental protection.
