AB  - Due to the high complexity and randomness of PM2.5 concentration series and the large amount of data, existing PM2.5 concentration prediction models do not consider air quality data and meteorological data, there is a problem of low prediction accuracy. Therefore, this paper proposes a PM2.5 concentration prediction model using improved LSTM in the big data environment. Firstly, original PM2.5 mass concentration sequences are decomposed by complementary ensemble empirical mode decomposition method. Then, Adam algorithm is applied to optimize the weight of long short-term memory neural network (LSTM). Finally, the sequence data is used as the input variable of improved LSTM model, and final PM2.5 concentration prediction results are obtained by deep learning. Based on the sampling data of monitoring points in Hohhot, simulation experiment is conducted on PM2.5 concentration prediction model. Experimental results show that the proposed model can significantly reduce prediction errors by considering air quality data and meteorological data. Compared with other models, the PM2.5 concentration prediction effect of proposed model is the best, and its root mean square error is only 8.769.
