AB  - AI-doped ZnO films were grown on different orientation sapphire substrates;(sapphire-R, C, M, A) at 400-600 degrees C via the atmospheric pressure aerosol-assisted MOCVD techriique. The influence of deposition temperature arid orientation of sapphire substrate on the microstructure, electrical and optical properties of ZnO-Al films was investigated, Epitaxial films grown on sapphire-R sub a es exhibited the best electrical properties: carrier mobility as 50-60 cm(2) V(-1)s(-1), resistivity <10(-3) Omega cm. The conditions post-deposition treatment of films (gas atmosphere during film cooling after deposition, ex-situ annealing) had a marked influence on the electrical properties of films,
